<%#
  The honeypot and the signed render timestamp, shared by every public form so the two
  checks can't drift apart or be forgotten on a new one. Include it inside the form
  element, using an unescaped include tag (see views/contact-us-form.ejs for the example
  — an EJS comment can't contain a closing tag, so it isn't repeated here).

  The honeypot is named `contactUrl` rather than anything resembling "honeypot", so a bot
  matching on field names wants to fill it. It is hidden three ways — off-screen, zero
  opacity, not tabbable — rather than with `type="hidden"`, because the better bots skip
  hidden inputs and fill visible ones. `autocomplete="off"` keeps a browser's autofill from
  putting a URL in it and getting a real person rejected.

  See utils/spamChecks.js for what the server does with them, and middleware/spamGate.js
  for why a rejection looks like a success.
%>
<div aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute; left:-9999px; top:auto; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; opacity:0;">
  <label for="<%= spamHoneypotField %>">Leave this field empty</label>
  <input type="text" id="<%= spamHoneypotField %>" name="<%= spamHoneypotField %>"
         value="" autocomplete="off" tabindex="-1">
</div>
<input type="hidden" name="formTs" value="<%= spamFormStamp %>">
